million in the same time period that the vulture population was rapidly declining in the 1990s and early 2000s. And Roman, I don't know if you know this, but vultures only ever go after dead things. They never attack the living. Yeah, but I imagine dogs do. Dogs do. They actually prey on the living. Dogs also transmit rabies, and in India, rabies is a real concern. It's been a real concern for a long time. India has the highest number of rabies related deaths in the world. There's a very strong correlation between the decline in vultures and the

